{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-frobenius-simplification","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:frobenius-simplification","kind":"remark","title":"Frobenius structure of the C gauge algebra","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-frobenius-pairing","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-instanton","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-irreducible-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-torsion-existence"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-universe","tags":["frobenius","hopf-algebra","gauge-theory"],"text":"frobenius-simplification.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:frobenius-simplification\"></a><p>The Haar state <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h_q</code> induces a non-degenerate Frobenius pairing on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}_q(\\mathrm{SU}(2))</code>. The non-degeneracy of the Frobenius form forces <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^0(M, \\mathrm{Ad}(A)) = 0</code>, as any global parallel section in the adjoint representation would pair with itself against the irreducibility constraint.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-simplification.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.25.9"}
